20. Limitations, Procedures, Instructions 
(a) The applicant should record the FGS operating limitations, procedures, and other information necessary 
for the safe operation of the aircraft in the Aircraft Flight Manual (AFM), in accordance with SC 
VTOL.2620 ‘Aircraft Flight Manual’. 
(b) This may include –but not be limited to– the following: 

minimum use height (for each applicable flight phase, operational procedure, FGS outer loops 
mode); 

applicable operations; 

flight envelop restrictions; 

configuration restrictions; 

external environmental conditions restrictions (e.g., icing, wind speed);
